WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.890
Idea. I am thinking of two numbers. Two clues, the sum and the difference, give exactly one answer. Two unknowns need two equations, solved together. These are simultaneous equations.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:25.173
In algebra the unknowns are constants in a polynomial, such as a and b. The remainder theorem says: divide f of x by x minus a, and the remainder is f of a.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:35.529
Each piece of information gives one equation. A factor gives f of the number equals zero. A remainder gives f of the number equals that remainder.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:48.301
The question gives two conditions, and asks you to show one constant, and find the other. Show that means the value is printed, and you must prove it. Reach the value by solving. Do not assume it.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:01:01.147
Method. Step one: for a factor, substitute the root and set it equal to zero. Step two: for a remainder, substitute the same way, and set it equal to the remainder.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:09.101
Step three: simplify each equation. Step four: solve them together. Step five: check in one condition.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.936
The trap is a sign slip with a negative value such as minus three. Use brackets.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:31.462
Worked example. January twenty twenty two. f of x has constants a and b. The bracket x plus two is a factor. The remainder on dividing by x plus three is twenty one. Show that a is two, and find b. Five marks.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:43.868
The factor x plus two means f of minus two is zero. Substitute: that is minus twenty four a plus sixteen b equals zero. Divide by eight: two b equals three a.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:55.275
The remainder twenty one on x plus three means f of minus three equals twenty one. Substitute: minus fifty one a, plus forty one b, equals twenty one.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:08.160
Solve together. From the first, b is three a over two. Substitute into the second. Twenty one a over two equals twenty one. So a is two, as required. Then b is three.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:18.831
A tempting wrong route is x equals three for the bracket x plus three. Then a comes out as fourteen over seventy five, not two. Make the bracket zero.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:33.020
So a equals two and b equals three. Check both clues. f of minus two is zero, and f of minus three is twenty one. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:43.783
Common mistake. A common mistake is to mix up a factor and a remainder. A remainder of twenty one gives f equals twenty one, not zero.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:54.679
Your turn. Now you try, from November twenty twenty. Find the value of p and the value of q. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:09.671
Answer. f of one is minus twelve, so p plus q is minus thirteen. f of four is thirty, so sixty four plus four p plus q equals thirty. That is four p plus q equals minus thirty four.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:27.913
Subtract the first equation from the second. Three p equals minus twenty one, so p is minus seven. Then q is minus six. Check: one minus seven minus six is minus twelve, and sixty four minus twenty eight minus six is thirty. Both clues work.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:37.684
The common wrong answer uses x equals minus one and minus four. That gives p equals minus thirty five. Make each bracket zero.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.893
Remember: one equation per clue, simplify, solve together, and check.
